[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

; `local_coords` under a SCALED emitter, the one place the flag is visible in a
; still frame. Both emitters carry the same scale = Vector2(3, 3) and the same
; particle settings; the global-coords one (Godot's default) draws its quads at
; the texture's own pixel size because Godot spawns in canvas space and draws
; the item with an identity transform, while the local-coords one is scaled up
; by its node like any other CanvasItem.
;
; `preprocess = 0.95`, not `1.0`: with `lifetime = 1.0` a preprocess of exactly
; one lifetime lands the settle right on the cycle's own wrap instant, where
; the whole stream has just recycled back toward the origin — a degenerate
; instant for ANY emitter, not something this fixture's own variable
; (`local_coords`) produces. 0.95 is the same window the other unauthored-
; preprocess fixture in this slice settles to, off that boundary.

